{
  "dom_id": "step-q171412",
  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "Express $A⇔B$ as a sentence given the following:\n\n- $A:$ $4$ is even.\n\n- $B:$ $4$ is divisible by $2.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the correct grammatical construction of $A⇔B$ is the following:\n\n$\\,$ $4$ is even **if and only if** $4$ is divisible by $2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
